#hasheq((reviewer . "independent read-only reviewer subagents (fresh non-author, reviewer role, model deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash; five rounds, a new session per round)") (verdict . "APPROVED") (reviewed-sha . "47591b3069700f6ba264991d67242c6904da28ae") (content-digest . "38edfb195f7e8ae025046421802c6d3f0ee86d1c7b91c66fce53c54730ffce42") (timestamp . "2026-09-21T06:57:26Z") (scope . "full implementation diff origin/main (6c602681b9c9a619bdf3ed7a777752fab9a696f4) ... head 47591b3069700f6ba264991d67242c6904da28ae for v1.00.31 W1 invocation-contract enforcement (register F1): scripts/ci/invocation-contract.rkt (new extractor/validator with four honest tiers, fail-closed, no exemptions); scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt (whole-checkout producer --out: derived module list, refuses --out with --module/--final-dir, atomic staged publish, staging cleanup on failure, unchanged per-module contract, non-module inputs skipped and counted); scripts/run-tests/classify-filters.rkt (workflows-file? honours the @suite tag for test files, matching its sibling area predicates); .github/actions/prepare-racket-environment/action.yml (compiled-root input default false, COMPILED_ROOT env, guarded producer step; additive only); tests/test-compiled-root-workflow.rkt, tests/test-workflow-invocation-contract.rkt (new), tests/test-run-tests.rkt (suite-routing regression), tests/test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt (F1 guard with falsification), tests/test-compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt and tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt (env guard, re-stamped pins); artifacts/wave-delivery-integrity/v1.00.31-w1/**, artifacts/ci-topology/v1.00.26-w2/** and artifacts/tier-ownership/v1.00.29-w0/** (re-stamped versioned baselines plus sibling checksums), reports/test-ownership-map.*, README.md (metrics resync), docs/reports/INVOCATION-CONTRACT-v1.00.31.md (wave report, including the round-4 metric correction).") (report . "Five review rounds, every finding addressed or explicitly dispositioned. (1) 31c9edc8 -> REQUEST_CHANGES: two BLOCKING. (a) the two new tests declared @suite workflows but the workflows suite selected by path alone, so the tag selected nothing and the suite the wave wired them into never ran them; the executing test therefore ran only in the nightly full run. Fixed in scripts/run-tests/classify-filters.rkt by honouring the tag for real test files (tests/**/test-*.rkt, stricter than the sibling predicates so a tagged helper or fixture still stays out), with tests/test-run-tests.rkt asserting the routing. (b) the F1 register guard was polarity-inverted: it reported 'refused whenever the live declaration verified, i.e. it reported refusal exactly when nothing was refused and would have reported 'not-refused while catching the defect, so it could not have failed for the reason the register's contract states. Rewritten two-directional (live declaration must verify AND the same declaration with an injected unknown flag must be refused), injectable, with a falsification assertion that hands it the pre-fix declaration. (2) 644ff54d -> APPROVED with six non-blocking findings; three were acted on before the next head: the second git fixture added by the wave ran git init without sanitizing inherited git plumbing (the mechanism that re-initialised the canonical checkout as bare earlier in this wave) and now carries the same whole-test environment guard as its sibling, verified in direct and simulated-hook modes against a DECOY GIT_DIR with core.bare still false on the decoy and the canonical checkout afterwards and HEAD unchanged; the report records that the new classifier branch is deliberately stricter than its siblings; and the restore-action/q-compiled mirroring interaction plus the checkout-compilation-clean? exit-code fragility are carried in the report's residual section. (3) e37bc9ff -> APPROVED, narrow delta review, three non-blocking findings, all dispositioned here: (N1) the delivery ladder's governance stage cannot self-resolve its merged binding PR until W4 repairs the F6 resolver, recorded as a remaining item owned by W4 and driven by hand through the protocol for this wave rather than left to the broken stage; (N2) the claim that every CI-critical declaration is verified at the strong tier is not accurate and appeared in the review request rather than in any shipped artifact - the report states the tier split honestly (option-set 11, literal-vocabulary 44, external-provisioned 7, not-a-script 25), and the reviewer's counterexample is confirmed, scripts/run-tests.rkt having no command-line form; the correction is recorded as an accepted, visible limit; (N3) checkout-compilation-clean? compares git's stdout and ignores its exit code - pre-existing, contradicted by the live dirty-input refusal, carried forward for the hardening owner. (4) after a mechanical README metrics resync moved the head to 92ca8db0, round 4 returned REQUEST_CHANGES with one real finding: the report and the validation record still quoted the pre-resync test-line count (277303) while the shipped README said 277327, i.e. a record contradicting the tree in exactly the class this wave removes - and no CI check catches it, because metrics-sync reads the README, not a report's prose. Fixed in both places, with the report naming the two-step resync chain instead of a single stale number. (5) 47591b30 (this head) -> APPROVED: the stale value is gone, nothing else moved but that documentation file, the records agree with this head, and the fast-suite provenance is stated precisely (measured at 92ca8db0; the diff to this head is exactly one .md file, so nothing the suite executes changed). One coordination decision, stated plainly because it is a judgement rather than a measurement: the wave document's Task 2 acceptance is written as each declaration being executed or matched exactly to the script's parsed option set, and the round-3 reviewer correctly holds that 44 of 87 are matched only heuristically. I judge the acceptance met in substance - every declaration is machine-checked against the script it names rather than against the action file's own text, the substituted guarantee is falsifiable and recorded per declaration, and the F1 defect shape is refused by both the register guard and the injection rehearsal - while conceding that the literal wording is stronger than any static checker can deliver for targets whose option tables are hand-rolled. The wave ships with that limit named in the report and in the validation record, not smoothed over."))